                <pb facs="0574" n="500" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg500"/>

                <head>No. 15.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[Telegram at 3-o’clock p. m., <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1865-02-14">February 14,
                        1865</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">M. le Chargé d’Affaires des Etats Unis à Paris:</hi></p>
                <p>A blockade-runner steamer under English flag has entered Ferrol with men,
                    ammunition, and supplies for the Stonewall. This ship will be ready to sail
                    to-day. The Niagara is vigilant. The Sacramento is still at Lisbon in spite of
                    all my efforts,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>PERRY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
